32-bit guests in a window above 4 GB (FineWine, macOS)

Local patch. FEX does not accept AI-written code: this is not to be sent upstream.

macOS gives a native arm64 process no memory below 4 GB, so a 32-bit guest cannot have the
addresses it uses. Its 4 GB are a window at FEX_GUEST_BASE instead (see the Wine side,
patches/runtime/0043). The base is a multiple of 4 GB: a host address in the window cut to 32
bits is the guest address, and the other way round is OR-ing the base in.

Only the WOW64 build (32-bit guests on an ARM64 Wine) has a base. In the ARM64EC build, which
runs x64 programs, FEX_GUEST_BASE is 0 and every change below compiles to what was there before.

- FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Core/GuestBase.h: the base, GuestPtr() and GuestAddr().
- Arm64 JIT: every guest memory operation forms its host address in a scratch register (the
  guest address zero-extended, with the base). x19 and x24 are taken out of the 32-bit register
  pool for that. Push, Pop, MemSet and MemCpy, which return addresses, keep those as guest ones.
- Core: guest code is read through the window when it is decoded, checked and hashed.
- WOW64 module: the syscall bridge reads the guest's stack and return address through the
  window; guest addresses from the core become host addresses for the code tracker and back.

